{:id "0002-characters-and-about"
 :title "Characters and About pages from content data"

 :goal "The site gains its last two pages. characters/index.html renders
        one card per entry in content/characters.edn; about/index.html
        renders the paragraphs in content/about.edn. Every page's nav now
        lists Home, Comics, Characters, About, derived from one nav vector
        plus the page's depth — the per-page hand-built links that order
        0001 shipped are gone. Adding a character is: add one map to
        characters.edn, run `bb build`, commit. On the way, the figure
        layout defect shipped by order 0001 is fixed: the frame and the
        caption stack, and nothing overflows a phone-width viewport."

 :acceptance
 ["`bb build` writes characters/index.html and about/index.html (and
   regenerates index.html and comics/index.html for the new nav); all four
   are committed and a second `bb build` leaves `git status` clean"
  "characters/index.html shows five cards in file order — Nana, Joey, Jane,
   Mom, Dad — each with the name as a heading, the role line, the blurb
   verbatim, and a figure: <img src alt> when :image is set, otherwise the
   `Not inked yet.` placeholder with no <img>"
  "about/index.html renders every string in content/about.edn as one <p>
   each, in order, verbatim, under a heading `About`"
  "Every generated page's nav lists exactly Home, Comics, Characters, About
   in that order; on a page one directory below the root every nav, css,
   home, and image href is prefixed `../` except the page's own entry"
  "home-page and comics-page no longer build nav-links, css-href, or
   home-href themselves: page-chrome derives all of them from a single
   nav-links vector and a :depth, and episode/character figures get their
   image prefix from the same depth"
  "site/validate-characters returns {:ok? false :errors [{:name \"Joey\"
   :field :alt :message ...}]} for a character with :image and blank :alt,
   and for a blank :name, :role, or :blurb; build! throws ex-info with
   :type :lag/invalid-characters before writing anything"
  "build! no longer writes css/site.css: building into a temp directory
   creates no css/ directory, and :written is exactly [\"index.html\"
   \"comics/index.html\" \"characters/index.html\" \"about/index.html\"]"
  "Every order-0001 acceptance criterion still holds; existing tests change
   only where the nav refactor requires it"
  "All hrefs and srcs relative, no <script>, no external URL, doctype,
   lang, viewport, and <title> on every page — including the two new ones"
  "Tests cover: character validation (valid, missing alt, blank blurb),
   card rendering with and without image, characters page order, about
   page paragraph order, nav contents and depth prefixes on a root page and
   a nested page, build! writing all four pages and no css into a temp dir"
  "Figure markup, for episodes and characters alike: <figure> contains a
   frame element (the bordered box, holding either the <img> or the
   `Not inked yet.` placeholder text) followed by <figcaption> as its
   sibling (characters omit the figcaption); a test asserts this structure
   for an episode with an image, an episode without, and a character card"
  "CSS puts the border, min-height, and centering on the frame element,
   never on <figure>; the `.episode-figure.placeholder { display: flex }`
   rule from 0001 is gone; the frame and images are capped at 100% width"
  "At a 360px-wide viewport none of the four pages scrolls horizontally
   and the caption sits below the frame — the build agent verifies this by
   rendering each page with the headless Chromium at
   /opt/pw-browsers/chromium-*/chrome-linux/chrome (see :context) and says
   so in its summary"
  "`bb test` stays green"]

 :scope ["src/**" "test/**" "css/**" "index.html" "comics/**"
         "characters/**" "about/**"]

 :non-goals
 ["No per-character pages, no episode-to-character cross links"
  "No changes to the episode schema, validation, or content/episodes.edn"
  "No README, no deployment tooling, no images committed — placeholders are HTML+CSS"
  "No CSS overhaul: add only the rules the cards and the About prose need"
  "No JavaScript, no webfonts, no external requests"
  "Do not fix latest-episode on an empty episodes vector — that is a separate order"
  "Do not edit content/*.edn, .nojekyll, bb.edn, DESIGN.md, or PRODUCT.md"]

 :design "lag.site keeps its shape and grows two pages and one refactor.

          The refactor first, because both new pages need it:

            (def nav-links [{:label \"Home\"       :href \"index.html\"}
                            {:label \"Comics\"     :href \"comics/index.html\"}
                            {:label \"Characters\" :href \"characters/index.html\"}
                            {:label \"About\"      :href \"about/index.html\"}])

            page-chrome takes {:title :depth :body}. :depth is 0 for
            index.html and 1 for any <dir>/index.html. A private
            (prefix depth) -> \"\" | \"../\" is applied to css, home, nav,
            and image hrefs; a nav entry that points at the current page
            (its href equals the page's own path) becomes just
            \"index.html\". Nobody outside page-chrome computes a link.
            The figure helper takes the same prefix, so home-page passes
            depth 0 and comics-page depth 1 and nothing else changes.

          New pure functions:

            (validate-characters characters) -> {:ok? true}
                                              | {:ok? false :errors [{:name \"Joey\" :field :alt :message \"...\"}]}
              rules: :name, :role, :blurb non-blank strings; :image nil or
              string; :alt non-blank when :image is set. Collect every error.
            (character-card character prefix) -> [:article.character
                                                   [:h2 name] [:p.role role]
                                                   figure [:p.blurb blurb]]
              reusing the episode figure's image/placeholder shape — one
              authored figure helper, generalized over {:image :alt}, not
              a second copy. Card figures carry no figcaption.
            (characters-page characters) -> document, cards in input order
            (about-page paragraphs)      -> document: [:h2 \"About\"] then
                                            one [:p] per string, in order

          lag.build:

            (build! {:root \".\"})
              -> {:written [\"index.html\" \"comics/index.html\"
                            \"characters/index.html\" \"about/index.html\"]}

            reads content/episodes.edn, content/characters.edn, and
            content/about.edn under root; validates episodes and
            characters (about is a vector of non-blank strings — validate
            it inline, no new public fn); throws :lag/invalid-episodes or
            :lag/invalid-characters before writing anything; creates the
            characters/ and about/ directories; writes the four pages.
            Delete stylesheet-source and the css write entirely —
            css/site.css is hand-authored and lives only in git.

          Figure shape, one helper for both pages:

            [:figure.art
             [:div.frame (if image [:img {:src (str prefix image) :alt alt}]
                                   [:p.placeholder-text "Not inked yet."])]
             (when caption [:figcaption caption])]

            .frame carries the 2px ink border, the uneven border-radius,
            min-height for the placeholder, and centered text (display:grid;
            place-items:center, or block + text-align) with max-width:100%
            and overflow hidden; img is display:block; width:100%;
            height:auto. <figure> keeps margin:0 and nothing else. This
            replaces 0001's flex-on-the-figure rule, which put the
            figcaption in the same row as the placeholder text and let it
            overflow the viewport on phones.

          CSS: append rules for .character (name, role in the soft ink
          colour, figure, blurb) and for About prose (measure and
          paragraph spacing). Keep the existing rules as they are."

 :examples
 ["content as committed -> characters/index.html contains five
   <article class=\"character\"> in order Nana, Joey, Jane, Mom, Dad, each
   with a placeholder figure containing `Not inked yet.` and no <img>; its
   <link> href is `../css/site.css` and its nav hrefs are `../index.html`,
   `../comics/index.html`, `index.html`, `../about/index.html`"
  "index.html nav hrefs are `index.html`, `comics/index.html`,
   `characters/index.html`, `about/index.html`"
  "character {:name \"Joey\" :role \"Eleven\" :image \"images/characters/joey.png\" :alt \"\" :blurb \"...\"}
   -> (validate-characters ...) => {:ok? false :errors [{:name \"Joey\" :field :alt :message ...}]}
   and (build! ...) throws :lag/invalid-characters, writes nothing"
  "character with :image \"images/characters/nana.png\" on the characters
   page -> <img src=\"../images/characters/nana.png\" alt=\"...\">"
  "about.edn as committed -> about/index.html has an <h2>About</h2> and
   five <p> elements whose text equals the five strings, in order"
  "index.html rendered at 360px wide -> no horizontal scrollbar; the
   placeholder frame spans the column and `Not inked yet.` is centered
   inside it with the caption on its own line below the frame"]

 :context
 ["This order builds on the tree shipped by order 0001 (letsaigrandma PR #1,
   branch factory/0001-episodes-to-site): src/lag/site.clj, src/lag/build.clj,
   css/site.css, test/lag/site_test.clj, test/lag/build_test.clj. Read all
   five before planning"
  "site.clj today: home-page and comics-page each hand-build :nav-links,
   :css-href, :home-href and pass an image prefix string to episode-block.
   The 0001 review station flagged this duplication; this order removes it"
  "build.clj today has a private stylesheet-source var and spits
   css/site.css on every build. Remove both; the stylesheet is an input,
   not an output"
  "content/characters.edn and content/about.edn are committed inputs with
   deliberate copy — render verbatim, do not edit"
  "DESIGN.md — the doctrine; the review station judges against it.
   PRODUCT.md — characters and voice, if alt text or a heading needs judgement"
  "test/lag/test_runner.clj discovers test/**/*_test.clj; add tests to the
   existing files or new ones, never edit the runner"
  "characters/ and about/ do not exist yet; build! creates them with
   babashka.fs/create-dirs"
  "The site is a GitHub Pages *project* site under /letsaigrandma/, which
   is why every link is relative and depth-prefixed"
  "Foreman render check of 0001's output at 390px found the figure
   overflowing the viewport and the placeholder text sitting beside the
   caption. Cause: css/site.css has `.episode-figure.placeholder { display:
   flex; ... }` and the <figcaption> is a child of that figure, so it
   becomes a flex item that refuses to shrink. Fix the structure (frame
   element + sibling caption), not just the CSS"
  "To render a page headlessly: serve the repo root with
   `python3 -m http.server 8000 --bind 127.0.0.1 &` then
   `/opt/pw-browsers/chromium-*/chrome-linux/chrome --headless=new
   --no-sandbox --disable-gpu --window-size=360,900 --screenshot=/tmp/x.png
   http://127.0.0.1:8000/`; or evaluate document.documentElement.scrollWidth
   with --dump-dom equivalents. Kill the server when done"
  "content/episodes.edn: Episode 1 currently has :image nil; the artist
   will set it to comics/001-that-comma.png soon. Both states must render
   correctly on Home and Comics"]

 :budget-usd 12.0}
